Beckn Implementation Guide – Secured Loans Use Case

Introduction:
This document provides the implementation guideline for integrating secured loans purchase flow over the Beckn-enabled UKI Network. It defines the messaging flows, payload specifications, taxonomy usage, and other supporting configurations to enable seamless interoperability between Beckn Network Participants (BAPs and BPPs). It assumes the reader has a good overview of the Beckn network, its APIs, the overall structure of the schema etc.

Structure of the document:
Outcome Visualization - This is a pictorial or descriptive representation of the different use cases that are supported by the network.
Flow diagrams - This section provides a pictorial representation of the message flows that happen during the use case.
API Calls and Schema - This section provides details on the API calls and the schema of the message that is sent in the form of sample schemas.
Taxonomy and layer 2 configuration - This section provides details on the taxonomy, enumerations and any rules defined for either the use case or by the network.
Notes on writing/integrating with your own software - This section describes ways in which you can integrate (Becknify) your new or existing software
Links to downloadable resources - This section contains the downloadable files referenced in this document.
Sandbox Details - Sandbox links to BAP, Registry/Gateway and BPP.

Outcome Visualization:
Context
Sanjeev is the secretary of Jeevan FPO, a registered Farmer Producer Organization (FPO) based in Nashik. The FPO seeks a secured loan to invest in cold storage and bulk input procurement for the upcoming season. Instead of relying on manual loan outreach, Sanjeev uses a Beckn-enabled BAP on the UKI Network to explore structured credit options with proper documentation and due diligence.
Discovery
Sanjeev logs into the UKI-enabled Beckn BAP (Generic Consumer app).
He searches for “Agri Infrastructure Loans” in the BAP application.
BAP shows him a wide range of loan solutions provided by various lenders.
Sanjeev filters the loans:
Entity Type/Role: Farmer Collective (Other options: Agri Startups, Agri Enterprises, Individual Farmer)
Loan Type: Input / Output / Infrastructure
Loan Amount & Tenure
Special Tags: Women-led, MSME, SFAC Certified
Example Results
ColdChain Capital Loan by Samunnati
₹15L starting from 8.5% interest annual
UDYAM & Land Collateral 
Min 200 Shareholders 
7-day TAT 
Infra Growth Credit by AgriBank
₹20L starting from 9.25% interest annual
UDYAM & Land Collateral
Personal Guarantor
5-day TAT
Order
Jeevan, Secretary of the FPO evaluates his options and selects “ColdChain Capital Loan” on the consumer application.
BAP responds with the following requirements:
Eligibility checklist
Required certifications: UDYAM
Pre-sanction documentation list
Interest rates, charges, repayment plan
Jeevan is satisfied with the selected solution and proceeds to apply. 
Application form Includes: 
Applicant name
FPO PAN (for CIBIL check)
Registration certificate
Bank details
UDYAM certificate
Shareholder list
Authorized signatory KYC
Collateral details (e.g., asset documents, land ownership)
OTP verification 
Jeevan submits the form after verifying the details. 
He receives a Loan Application ID generated by the lender upon submission.
Fulfilment
After the submission, Jeevan can log into the consumer app and track his form status using the Loan Application ID.
Verification can fail if the FPO’s CIBIL score does not match the requirement.
Upon CIBIL verification, Jeevan uploads the additional documents needed.
Additional uploads:
Balance sheets
Bank statements 
Collateral verification docs
Board declarations
UDYAM certificate
Shareholder list
Authorized signatory KYC
Lender validates:
CIBIL, GST profile, asset ownership
Upon successful document validation:
The lender sends back a final loan quote and a sanction letter.
Sanjeev accepts terms digitally via Aadhaar eSign or OTP.
Loan amount becomes available for disbursement as per approved limits.
FPO can initiate disbursement request via app.
Loan is credited to the FPO’s verified bank account.
Post-Fulfilment
Jeevan submits a rating for the product that he has purchased. The seller receives the rating and can request for further feedback.
He can reach out to support services in case of any issues with the service delivery.


CANCEL:
Sanjeev cancels the loan pre approval by withdrawing his application, no charges were applied on him. The order was cancelled.
If he cancels, post approval, before disbursement, processing fee was charged.
If he cancels, post approval after disbursement was initiated, processing fee plus penalty was charged.

Flow Diagrams
General Beckn message flow and error handling.

This section is relevant to all the message flows illustrated below and discussed further in the document.

Beckn is a synchronous protocol at its core.

When a network participant(NP1) sends a message to another participant(NP2), the other participant(NP2) immediately returns back an ACK/NACK(Acknowledgement or Negative Acknowledgement in case of error - usually with wrongly formed messages).
An ACK is an indicator that the receiving participant(NP2) will process this message and dispatch an on_xxxxxx message to original NP (NP1)
Subsequently after processing the message NP2 sends back the real response in the corresponding on_xxxxxx message, to which again the first participant(NP1).
This message can contain a message field (for success) or error field (for failure)
NP1 when it receives the on_xxxxxx message, sends back an ACK/NACK (Here in both the cases NP1 will not send any subsequent message).
In the Use case diagrams, this ACK/NACK is not illustrated explicitly to keep the diagrams crisp.
However when writing software we should be prepared to receive these NACK messages as well as error field in the on_xxxxxx messages
While this discussion is from a Beckn perspective, Adapters can provide synchronous modes. For example, the Protocol Server which is the reference implementation of the Beckn Adapter provides a synchronous mode by default. So if your software calls the support endpoint on the BAP Protocol Server, the Protocol Server waits till it gets the on_support and returns back that as the response.



Structure of a message with a NACK

```
{
    "message": {
        "ack": {
            "status": "NACK"
        }
    },
    "error": {
        "code": 400,
        "message": "OpenApiValidator Error at BAP-CLIENT",
    }
}
```

Structure of a on_select message with an error
```
{
    "context": {
        "action": "on_select",
        "version": "1.1.0",
        ...
    },
    "error": {
        "code": 30001,
        "message": "Requested provider is not in the database"
    }
}
```

API Calls and Schema
1. search
Purpose: Sanjeev initiates discovery of available credit offerings for agri-infra loans suitable for FPOs.
Request Payload:
{
    "context": {
        "domain": "credit-services:uki",
        "action": "search",
        "version": "1.1.0",
        "bap_id": "credit-fpo.bap.uki.in",
        "bap_uri": "https://credit-fpo.bap.uki.in",
        "transaction_id": "3a5b0b23-501e-42e8-b43b-03b60e822882",
        "message_id": "89b7fa3e-5df6-40dc-b457-0a8a986b7603",
        "ttl": "PT10M",
        "timestamp": "2025-06-02T10:00:00Z",
        "location": {
            "city": {
                "code": "std:95253"
            },
            "country": {
                "code": "IND"
            }
        }
    },
    "message": {
        "intent": {
            "descriptor": {
                "name": "Agri Infrastructure Loan"
            },
            "tags": [
                {
                    "descriptor": {
                        "name": "eligibility"
                    },
                    "list": [
                        {
                            "descriptor": {
                                "code": "entity-type"
                            },
                            "value": "farmer-collective"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "descriptor": {
                        "name": "financial-terms"
                    },
                    "list": [
                        {
                            "descriptor": {
                                "code": "loan-type"
                            },
                            "value": "infrastructure"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    }
}

