Notes on Writing/Integrating with Your Own Software:
This section provides guidance on how you would integrate your own software with the Beckn-enabled UKI Network, using the Beckn-ONIX initiative and sandbox environments.
Overview: Beckn-ONIX
Beckn-ONIX is a framework that enables easy installation, configuration, and operation of a Beckn Network. It provides necessary protocol server implementations and adapters for quick onboarding to a network like UKI.
Reference: Beckn-ONIX Repository
Integrating the Seeker Platform
If you are building a Seeker Platform (BAP client):
Identify the supported use cases from this document relevant to your app.
Design and develop the UI to support the required flows.
The UI will interact with an API Server (your application backend).
The API Server must:
Create JSON request payloads as per API schemas.
Manage API callbacks and validate incoming Beckn responses.
Install the BAP Protocol Server using Beckn-ONIX reference implementation.
Configure the following during installation:
Registry Address (Sandbox or Production)
Subscriber URL (where callbacks are received)
subscriber_id (same as URL without 'https://')
Load the correct Layer 2 configuration file for insurance:uki.
Coordinate with UKI Network Tech Support to whitelist your BAP Subscriber.
After activation, you can transact fully on the sandbox.
Once functional, move toward pre-production and production following the Starter Kit instructions.
Integrating the Provider Platform
If you are building a Provider Platform (BPP server):
Identify the supported use cases and flows from this document.
Create a Webhook Endpoint in your server (for search, select, confirm, etc.).
Install the BPP Protocol Server from the Beckn-ONIX repository.
Configure during installation:
Registry Address (Sandbox or Production)
Subscriber URL (where callbacks are received)
subscriber_id (same as URL without 'https://')
Webhook URL (your server's endpoint URL)
Configure your server to:
Accept Beckn requests.
Send synchronous ACKs.
Forward and manage on_ callbacks.
Load the Layer 2 file relevant for insurance:uki.
Coordinate with network administrators to enable your BPP on the registry.
Use sandbox-provided Postman collection to test your BPP endpoints.
After sandbox testing, progress to production onboarding.

